WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.340 --> 00:00:05.570
In the long history of the world, the planet
has played host to a wide variety of ancient

00:00:05.570 --> 00:00:06.860
civilizations.

00:00:06.860 --> 00:00:11.320
There are far, far too many of those for any
one video to cover - people make it their

00:00:11.320 --> 00:00:16.350
careers to discover and catalog the civilizations
that preceded us in the modern era.

00:00:16.350 --> 00:00:20.140
Archaeologists and historians make it their
life’s work to learn everything there is

00:00:20.140 --> 00:00:25.430
to know about these mighty empires and kingdoms
that spanned vast swaths of land where there

00:00:25.430 --> 00:00:27.470
are now dozens of countries.

00:00:27.470 --> 00:00:32.029
A lot of these civilizations are famous: even
schoolchildren know about them.

00:00:32.029 --> 00:00:34.700
Take the Roman empire, for example.

00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:39.300
Everyone knows about the mighty Roman Empire
- Julius Caesar took control of the Roman

00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:43.200
Republic and created the empire that would
go on to be one of the the largest empires

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:44.649
in history at the time.

00:00:44.649 --> 00:00:50.040
It controlled practically everything in Europe
and North Africa, and even parts of Asia.

00:00:50.040 --> 00:00:55.250
The Romans made amazing advancements in culture,
architecture, law, and practically everything

00:00:55.250 --> 00:00:56.250
else.

00:00:56.250 --> 00:01:00.980
In fact, their legacy can even be seen in
pop culture today - the American Senate is

00:01:00.980 --> 00:01:05.829
modeled off the Roman Senate, and practically
every nation in the world has their own kind

00:01:05.829 --> 00:01:08.650
of wine - a Roman invention.

00:01:08.650 --> 00:01:10.329
Or take the Macedonian Empire.

00:01:10.329 --> 00:01:14.539
A lot of people don’t know it’s name,
but you almost definitely know the person

00:01:14.539 --> 00:01:17.749
who created it - Alexander the Great.

00:01:17.749 --> 00:01:20.549
At only twenty, he took his father’s throne.

00:01:20.549 --> 00:01:25.229
Then he began launching military expeditions,
and it soon became clear that young Alexander

00:01:25.229 --> 00:01:27.249
was a brilliant tactician.

00:01:27.249 --> 00:01:32.340
Never defeated in battle, he managed to extend
his vast empire across all of West Asia and

00:01:32.340 --> 00:01:36.630
North Africa, stretching all the way to Egypt
and India.

00:01:36.630 --> 00:01:41.090
Like Caesar would go on to do after him, he
managed to create one of the largest empires

00:01:41.090 --> 00:01:45.399
in history, except he did it all before he
even turned thirty.

00:01:45.399 --> 00:01:50.389
Though he died young and his empire was split
apart by his generals, he brought Greek thought,

00:01:50.389 --> 00:01:56.020
culture, and philosophy - not to mention science
- to the far reaches of inner Asia.

00:01:56.020 --> 00:02:01.380
And of course there is the Mongol empire,
led by the fearsome Genghis Khan.

00:02:01.380 --> 00:02:05.709
The Mongols, a nomadic people from central
Asia, were divided into dozens of distinct

00:02:05.709 --> 00:02:09.289
tribes until Genghis Khan united them under
one flag.

00:02:09.289 --> 00:02:15.700
And from there, they spread outward violently
into the rest of Asia, conquering China, Korea,

00:02:15.700 --> 00:02:19.160
Eastern Europe, and practically all of Asia.

00:02:19.160 --> 00:02:23.989
In doing so, they created the largest empire
in history, and killed somewhere near 40 million

00:02:23.989 --> 00:02:28.489
people in their conquests - ten percent of
the world’s population at the time!

00:02:28.489 --> 00:02:32.930
But they also created a safe trade route from
China to Europe, what is now known as the

00:02:32.930 --> 00:02:34.129
Silk Road.

00:02:34.129 --> 00:02:38.410
And their innovations with cavalry would go
on to inform warfare using horses for the

00:02:38.410 --> 00:02:40.680
next 800 years.

00:02:40.680 --> 00:02:43.719
Moving out of Asia, there are also the legendary
Mayans.

00:02:43.719 --> 00:02:48.879
The Mayans were more of a loose confederation
of different tribes, working together to advance

00:02:48.879 --> 00:02:50.219
a common civilization.

00:02:50.219 --> 00:02:55.010
They didn’t conquer as much land as the
others, only one area in Central America,

00:02:55.010 --> 00:03:00.609
but they crafted a complex society with laws,
civic duties, social rules, and extremely

00:03:00.609 --> 00:03:03.170
advanced religious rites and architecture.

00:03:03.170 --> 00:03:07.731
If you go to South America today, you can
still see the remnants of their empire: step

00:03:07.731 --> 00:03:12.950
pyramids that look sort of like ziggurats,
deep in the South American jungle interior.

00:03:12.950 --> 00:03:19.010
They invented astronomy, calendars, writing,
and many forms of art like mosaics - all without

00:03:19.010 --> 00:03:21.280
any contact with European society.

00:03:21.280 --> 00:03:25.560
Needless to say, the advancements empires
have made through history are so important

00:03:25.560 --> 00:03:28.530
we use them in our daily lives all the time.

00:03:28.530 --> 00:03:32.459
And we know a lot about these ancient empires,
too - how could we not?

00:03:32.459 --> 00:03:37.440
They’ve made massive impacts on the planet
and population, not to even mention religion,

00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:39.700
culture, law - society as a whole.

00:03:39.700 --> 00:03:44.150
But what if there was an empire on the planet
that was larger and more advanced than all

00:03:44.150 --> 00:03:45.670
of the ones we just looked through.

00:03:45.670 --> 00:03:50.080
And not just more advanced by a little bit
- so advanced that they were creating nuclear

00:03:50.080 --> 00:03:54.920
reactors well before Alexander was taking
his first steps or Plutarch was trying to

00:03:54.920 --> 00:03:56.999
complete a history of the Greeks.

00:03:56.999 --> 00:04:01.170
So advanced that we still don’t totally
understand what they were capable of.

00:04:01.170 --> 00:04:03.650
I’d certainly call that anomalous, would
you?

00:04:03.650 --> 00:04:08.829
And that’s not all - what if this empire
also managed to stay hidden from modern science

00:04:08.829 --> 00:04:09.829
for centuries?

00:04:09.829 --> 00:04:14.930
They didn’t stay alive, but their ruins
have never been found by the scientific community.

00:04:14.930 --> 00:04:18.620
Their relics have been squirreled away from
the eyes of the world over the decades.

00:04:18.620 --> 00:04:24.680
You’d never find a reference to the “Mekhanite
Empire” in a history textbook or in a museum,

00:04:24.680 --> 00:04:26.850
and that’s for a very good reason.

00:04:26.850 --> 00:04:31.979
The SCP Foundation has spent an extremely
large amount of time and money ensuring that

00:04:31.979 --> 00:04:36.569
the evidence of this ancient empire never
comes out to the rest of the world.

00:04:36.569 --> 00:04:41.979
But even if a culture creates anomalies, is
the culture itself anomalous?

00:04:41.979 --> 00:04:45.950
Does it need to be contained, especially if
they’re all long dead and their technology

00:04:45.950 --> 00:04:48.220
has degraded into unusability?

00:04:48.220 --> 00:04:53.259
Well, maybe… except their technology is
doing just fine.

00:04:53.259 --> 00:04:58.900
Two thousand years and counting, their technology
is still working perfectly - in some cases,

00:04:58.900 --> 00:05:00.990
better than our modern devices.

00:05:00.990 --> 00:05:02.569
How can that be possible?

00:05:02.569 --> 00:05:04.419
How can that not be anomalous?

00:05:04.419 --> 00:05:07.560
Well, as unbelievable as it might seem, it’s
true.

00:05:07.560 --> 00:05:12.110
We’ll dive more into what exactly this empire
out of Greece was in a bit, but for now we’re

00:05:12.110 --> 00:05:15.699
going to look at an SCP file associated with
them.

00:05:15.699 --> 00:05:19.800
Except this one couldn’t be picked up, stuffed
in a box, and shipped off to a containment

00:05:19.800 --> 00:05:21.110
locker in Site-19.

00:05:21.110 --> 00:05:26.360
You’ll see why in a minute, but for now,
let’s take a look at the file.

00:05:26.360 --> 00:05:32.070
SCP-2406 lacks any images or flashy documentation,
so no clues there.

00:05:32.070 --> 00:05:33.070
Unless…

00:05:33.070 --> 00:05:36.930
it’s not possible to photograph the anomaly
for some reason.

00:05:36.930 --> 00:05:37.930
Hmm.

00:05:37.930 --> 00:05:42.030
The object class is safe, and the containment
procedures aren’t very long.

00:05:42.030 --> 00:05:48.229
A site, Provisional Site-31, has been constructed
around SCP-2406 and is under the cover of

00:05:48.229 --> 00:05:50.500
a Kazakhstani military base.

00:05:50.500 --> 00:05:55.020
Provisional Sites are temporary sites that
the Foundation puts up in the field to contain

00:05:55.020 --> 00:05:59.610
an anomaly that can’t easily be transported
somewhere else for containment.

00:05:59.610 --> 00:06:05.050
And if its a Kazakhstani military facility,
the anomaly is probably somewhere in Kazakhstan

00:06:05.050 --> 00:06:07.139
and can’t be moved.

00:06:07.139 --> 00:06:08.510
Seems reasonable enough.

00:06:08.510 --> 00:06:14.229
All personnel who work directly with SCP-2406
are required to wear a Type-A Hazmat Suit

00:06:14.229 --> 00:06:19.639
when in contact with the anomaly, and to undergo
a full decontamination bath upon exiting.

00:06:19.639 --> 00:06:25.409
Whatever SCP-2406 is, being in direct contact
with it can be dangerous to humans, so the

00:06:25.409 --> 00:06:30.580
Foundation uses specialized hazardous material
suits - the big yellow jumpsuits you see near

00:06:30.580 --> 00:06:35.410
radiation or chemical spill sites.On top of
that, an armed contingent of guards are to

00:06:35.410 --> 00:06:41.600
remain in place in and around Provisional
Site-31 to ensure no one unauthorized accesses

00:06:41.600 --> 00:06:42.600
the anomaly.

00:06:42.600 --> 00:06:47.789
Though you’d have to wonder why anyone would
try to access a military base…

00:06:47.789 --> 00:06:52.500
The containment procedures close out by declaring
that anyone wanting to directly interact with

00:06:52.500 --> 00:06:59.060
SCP-2406-1, whatever it is, needs to get authorization
from their Site Director.

00:06:59.060 --> 00:07:04.000
So SCP-2406 has at least one subanomaly to
deal with.

00:07:04.000 --> 00:07:09.069
Obviously, the Foundation is very interested
in keeping this anomaly - or these anomalies

00:07:09.069 --> 00:07:14.760
- secret and protected at all costs, as well
as limiting human exposure to something potentially

00:07:14.760 --> 00:07:15.760
dangerous.

00:07:15.760 --> 00:07:18.220
Now, let’s take a look at the Description:

00:07:18.220 --> 00:07:25.860
SCP-2046 is a mechanical automaton that’s
93 meters tall and weighs approximately 210

00:07:25.860 --> 00:07:27.080
metric tonnes.

00:07:27.080 --> 00:07:33.919
For the Americans among us, that’s about
300 feet in height and 230 tons - over 450,000

00:07:33.919 --> 00:07:35.189
pounds!

00:07:35.189 --> 00:07:37.449
No wonder the Foundation couldn’t move it.

00:07:37.449 --> 00:07:42.689
After investigating, research has concluded
that SCP-2406 wasn’t sentient, so it wasn’t

00:07:42.689 --> 00:07:45.560
a robot or cyborg or artificial intelligence.

00:07:45.560 --> 00:07:51.669
An automaton is a machine to perform a specific
task - and this thing, whatever it is, was

00:07:51.669 --> 00:07:55.870
controlled by at least six different operators,
if not more.

00:07:55.870 --> 00:08:01.530
They piloted the machine using 160 different
valves and levers within the torso, head and

00:08:01.530 --> 00:08:03.259
chest of the automaton.

00:08:03.259 --> 00:08:08.259
And if it has a head and chest, it has limbs
- limbs that were controlled by a combination

00:08:08.259 --> 00:08:11.819
of pneumatics, hydraulics, and clockwork machinery.

00:08:11.819 --> 00:08:15.759
But controlling it is one thing - how the
heck does something like this get the power

00:08:15.759 --> 00:08:16.879
to move?

00:08:16.879 --> 00:08:22.129
The answer is a nuclear reactor embedded in
its torso with power cables running to its

00:08:22.129 --> 00:08:23.380
arms and legs.

00:08:23.380 --> 00:08:28.969
Yep, unbelievable as it may seem, this ancient
curiosity was powered by the same source our

00:08:28.969 --> 00:08:33.420
modern aircraft carriers and nuclear submarines
use.

00:08:33.420 --> 00:08:41.200
SCP-2406 was discovered on August 7, 1985
in the Aralkum Desert - but not by the Foundation.

00:08:41.200 --> 00:08:45.570
The Aralkum desert used to be part of the
Aral Sea before the Soviets drained part of

00:08:45.570 --> 00:08:51.450
it - it was during one of these drainings
that the Russian military discovered SCP-2406,

00:08:51.450 --> 00:08:53.830
by tracking the radiation coming from it.

00:08:53.830 --> 00:08:58.010
As soon as they realized what they found wasn’t
some sort of abandoned warhead or uranium

00:08:58.010 --> 00:09:03.270
deposit, they called in the GRU’s P-Division
- the unit of the Soviet government who dealt

00:09:03.270 --> 00:09:06.600
with anomalies, in the same way the Foundation
did.

00:09:06.600 --> 00:09:10.280
They kept custody of the anomaly, but only
for a few years.

00:09:10.280 --> 00:09:15.690
When the USSR collapsed in 1991, the Foundation
stepped in with their agents and took control

00:09:15.690 --> 00:09:20.650
of the anomaly while everyone else in the
area was busy dealing with the political fallout.

00:09:20.650 --> 00:09:25.780
They immediately began performing research,
and learned that the material SCP-2406 is

00:09:25.780 --> 00:09:32.150
made up of isn’t just one metal, but a toughened
alloy of copper, zinc, nickel, lead, and iron.

00:09:32.150 --> 00:09:37.320
That mixture is why the metal looks bronze,
despite not having any bronze in it.

00:09:37.320 --> 00:09:39.620
They also found two markings on it.

00:09:39.620 --> 00:09:43.600
One was on the outside of its back, and showed
the Aegean numeral for “9”.

00:09:43.600 --> 00:09:47.480
Does that mean there are at least 8 more of
these things buried somewhere?

00:09:47.480 --> 00:09:50.540
Maybe, but the Foundation hasn’t found any
of them.

00:09:50.540 --> 00:09:56.490
What’s more interesting is that the numeral
is Aegean, Greek, despite SCP-2406 lying in

00:09:56.490 --> 00:10:00.040
a lake in the Aral sea, pretty far from Greece.

00:10:00.040 --> 00:10:04.720
The front of the anomaly, its chest, has an
intricate symbol of a hammer striking an anvil

00:10:04.720 --> 00:10:05.720
on it.

00:10:05.720 --> 00:10:10.030
The right arm of the anomaly has a nozzle
with piping attached to it - the piping leads

00:10:10.030 --> 00:10:14.480
to a pressurized chamber within SCP-2409 that
is empty.

00:10:14.480 --> 00:10:19.190
But the Foundation did manage to find trace
residue of various chemicals, such as pine

00:10:19.190 --> 00:10:25.460
resin, naphtha, quicklime, calcium phosphide,
and sulfur, inside of the corners of the tank.

00:10:25.460 --> 00:10:30.750
Not coincidentally, those are the exact same
chemicals used to create Greek Fire, a primitive

00:10:30.750 --> 00:10:35.100
chemical weapon similar to napalm that the
ancient Greeks used in warfare.

00:10:35.100 --> 00:10:40.920
Between this and the Aegean numeral, the Foundation
judged that SCP-2406 was almost definitely

00:10:40.920 --> 00:10:44.460
constructed in Greece and brought here for
some reason.

00:10:44.460 --> 00:10:46.930
The left arm of the anomaly isn’t attached
to it.

00:10:46.930 --> 00:10:50.920
In fact, initial reports said it was torn
off at the shoulder and couldn’t be found

00:10:50.920 --> 00:10:55.520
with the rest of it, but it seems that the
Foundation managed to recover it since, detailed

00:10:55.520 --> 00:10:57.860
in one of the addenda in the file.

00:10:57.860 --> 00:11:02.740
Chemicals weren’t the only things they found
inside SCP-2406: when they busted the main

00:11:02.740 --> 00:11:07.590
access plate open, researchers found something
decidedly more morbid.

00:11:07.590 --> 00:11:12.320
Six different human skeletons located inside
its torso area were removed and cataloged

00:11:12.320 --> 00:11:17.780
before being carbon dated to 1100 BC - over
3000 years old!

00:11:17.780 --> 00:11:22.510
And they were all wearing an extremely strange
set of armor - while it looked Greek, it was

00:11:22.510 --> 00:11:26.720
made of a strange lead-copper alloy and filled
with asbestos lining.

00:11:26.720 --> 00:11:32.461
Presumably, the armor was designed to absorb
the radiation put out by SCP-2406’s reactor

00:11:32.461 --> 00:11:36.900
- there were also tubes from the helmets leading
to the outside, so that they could breathe

00:11:36.900 --> 00:11:38.220
safe air.

00:11:38.220 --> 00:11:42.820
One of the levers pumped water into the tubes
so that the pilots didn’t die of thirst,

00:11:42.820 --> 00:11:46.630
and another tube was near the groin, probably
so that they could pee.

00:11:46.630 --> 00:11:52.020
Seems like the designers ensured that whoever
was piloting SCP-2406 could do so for hours

00:11:52.020 --> 00:11:53.290
or days.

00:11:53.290 --> 00:11:58.890
The Foundation ensured through testing that
SCP-2406 doesn’t work - the limbs don’t

00:11:58.890 --> 00:12:01.990
move, and many of the levers have rusted or
broken.

00:12:01.990 --> 00:12:06.860
All of that damage from disuse is repairable,
but there is even more extensive damage from

00:12:06.860 --> 00:12:07.860
combat.

00:12:07.860 --> 00:12:12.480
The limbs and head were first discovered run
through by long, sharp spikes made of an unknown

00:12:12.480 --> 00:12:13.480
substance.

00:12:13.480 --> 00:12:17.830
Though it feels like chitin, its molecular
structure is closer to coral - and on top

00:12:17.830 --> 00:12:22.710
of that, it’s biological and contains some
elements of human DNA.

00:12:22.710 --> 00:12:27.560
Parts of its limbs are also crushed or indented
with a segmented pattern, like a Boa constrictor

00:12:27.560 --> 00:12:29.400
wrapping around its prey.

00:12:29.400 --> 00:12:35.399
The evidence suggests that SCP-2406 was in
an intense fight with some sort of giant monster

00:12:35.399 --> 00:12:36.710
- and lost.

00:12:36.710 --> 00:12:39.860
But that’s all in the past.

00:12:39.860 --> 00:12:43.590
SCP-2406 also has a more present problem:
its reactor.

00:12:43.590 --> 00:12:47.460
It melted through the back of the anomaly,
penetrating the Earth, and seems to still

00:12:47.460 --> 00:12:52.630
be burning incredibly hot and radioactive
nearly a kilometer under the surface.

00:12:52.630 --> 00:12:57.300
Engineers think that when it was intact, it
worked similarly to “natural” nuclear

00:12:57.300 --> 00:13:02.840
reactions rather than modern reactors, like
when a uranium deposit begins to undergo fission.

00:13:02.840 --> 00:13:08.220
If nothing else, it means that SCP-2406’s
designers were studying those, and were far

00:13:08.220 --> 00:13:12.530
more advanced scientifically than any other
culture on the face of the planet at the time

00:13:12.530 --> 00:13:14.160
- that we know of.

00:13:14.160 --> 00:13:18.940
When they were investigating the wreck, Foundation
personnel also discovered something interesting

00:13:18.940 --> 00:13:24.620
- a watertight ceramic jar, like the ones
Ancient Egyptians used to preserve organs.

00:13:24.620 --> 00:13:29.890
When they broke the seal, they found two tightly-bound
scrolls written in a unique language resembling

00:13:29.890 --> 00:13:31.210
Mycenaean Greek.

00:13:31.210 --> 00:13:36.570
It took ten years of research for the Foundation’s
best linguists to translate the scrolls.

00:13:36.570 --> 00:13:41.110
What they found confirmed their theory - the
scrolls were religious, and written by a group

00:13:41.110 --> 00:13:46.240
called the “Followers of Mekhane” - the
ancient precursors to what we now call the

00:13:46.240 --> 00:13:51.690
infamous Church of the Broken God, an anomalous
cult that seeks to rebuild their deity and

00:13:51.690 --> 00:13:53.930
make themselves more than human.

00:13:53.930 --> 00:13:57.720
The Foundation’s had run-ins with them in
the past, but the documents indicate that

00:13:57.720 --> 00:14:02.830
three thousand years ago, they weren’t just
a cult - they were an empire.

00:14:02.830 --> 00:14:05.260
The first scroll was translated to the following:

00:14:05.260 --> 00:14:08.110
The Colossi were constructed in Her Schema.

00:14:08.110 --> 00:14:12.230
The Colossi were constructed to [defend/secure/contain?].

00:14:12.230 --> 00:14:14.890
The Enemy: Grand Karcist Ion.

00:14:14.890 --> 00:14:16.650
Betrayer of Man.

00:14:16.650 --> 00:14:18.440
Destroyer of Progress.

00:14:18.440 --> 00:14:19.930
Sorcerer King of Adytum.

00:14:19.930 --> 00:14:27.420
A desolate domain, a failed and fallen creation,
built with the [bodies/flesh] of dead gods.

00:14:27.420 --> 00:14:30.640
Upon a throne of black ambition, the Enemy
plots.

00:14:30.640 --> 00:14:32.500
The Enemy is not a priest.

00:14:32.500 --> 00:14:34.140
They are a merchant.

00:14:34.140 --> 00:14:37.510
And they have sold the [world/whole/totality].

00:14:37.510 --> 00:14:40.000
The Colossi were constructed in Her Schema.

00:14:40.000 --> 00:14:43.700
The Colossi were constructed to [defend/secure/contain?].

00:14:43.700 --> 00:14:47.310
The Profane Tools must be [broken/"uncreated"].

00:14:47.310 --> 00:14:49.950
Drink deep the silver blood of MEKHANE.

00:14:49.950 --> 00:14:53.090
May Her sacrifice not [be in vain?].

00:14:53.090 --> 00:14:55.890
Strange, but definitely religious.

00:14:55.890 --> 00:14:59.580
It seems to be a dedication - to the Broken
God, Mekhane.

00:14:59.580 --> 00:15:03.680
The Colossi were created to fight their ancient
enemy, the Sarkics.

00:15:03.680 --> 00:15:06.660
But The second document is much more interesting:

00:15:06.660 --> 00:15:11.910
This is a testament of Matriarch Eupraxia,
Legates-Faithful, Servant of MEKHANE.

00:15:11.910 --> 00:15:14.410
I am not a warrior.

00:15:14.410 --> 00:15:16.100
But all warriors are dead.

00:15:16.100 --> 00:15:18.900
Breaking themselves upon the Enemy's host.

00:15:18.900 --> 00:15:21.770
The Enemy has set their plan into motion.

00:15:21.770 --> 00:15:23.980
The Sorcerer King surrounds himself with corpses.

00:15:23.980 --> 00:15:27.690
To fight, is to [grow/increase in number]
his legions.

00:15:27.690 --> 00:15:28.934
Egypt retreats from [the world/us/contact
with us].

00:15:28.934 --> 00:15:32.560
The Hittites have fallen into chaos.

00:15:32.560 --> 00:15:35.810
The Conspirators of Crete have sacrificed
their own.

00:15:35.810 --> 00:15:38.140
The Aegean has fallen into barbarism.

00:15:38.140 --> 00:15:41.800
[The city of a thousand pillars] is forever
lost.

00:15:41.800 --> 00:15:43.560
Has always been lost.

00:15:43.560 --> 00:15:47.110
Even the Daeva grow desperate with the enemy
at their border.

00:15:47.110 --> 00:15:50.080
The center collapses - kingdoms crumble.

00:15:50.080 --> 00:15:51.630
The damage is done.

00:15:51.630 --> 00:15:54.080
The light of reason [flickers/wanes].

00:15:54.080 --> 00:15:58.560
But MEKHANE sacrificed herself so that we
might be free.

00:15:58.560 --> 00:16:01.290
We refuse to return to that darkness.

00:16:01.290 --> 00:16:02.890
We would rather die.

00:16:02.890 --> 00:16:04.700
But the siege at Gyaros was won.

00:16:04.700 --> 00:16:06.890
We must strike while the metal is hot.

00:16:06.890 --> 00:16:11.320
And thus, we march for Kythera - at the end
of all things.

00:16:11.320 --> 00:16:13.890
We have crossed the wine-dark sea.

00:16:13.890 --> 00:16:16.710
We have seen villages ravaged by the Red Death.

00:16:16.710 --> 00:16:20.370
We have seen the dead, the dying, and the
deathless.

00:16:20.370 --> 00:16:23.020
We cast the accursed to holy flame.

00:16:23.020 --> 00:16:25.970
We enter his desolate domain.

00:16:25.970 --> 00:16:29.360
And in our left hand, we carry our ANSWER.

00:16:29.360 --> 00:16:34.320
We cannot undo what has been done - but we
can delay the Sarkic Dawn.

00:16:34.320 --> 00:16:39.220
So it seems that the ancient Mekhanite Empire
were once at war with another empire, the

00:16:39.220 --> 00:16:40.250
hated Sarkics.

00:16:40.250 --> 00:16:45.920
Losing and all their allies dying, they poured
their resources into these massive mechs and

00:16:45.920 --> 00:16:50.820
sent them deep into enemy territory equipped
with some sort of doomsday weapon as a hope

00:16:50.820 --> 00:16:52.110
for success.

00:16:52.110 --> 00:16:56.190
What happens next is, unfortunately, a mystery.

00:16:56.190 --> 00:17:03.110
On December 12th of 1998, the Foundation found
something almost 30 kilometres away from SCP-2406

00:17:03.110 --> 00:17:04.600
during a routine patrol.

00:17:04.600 --> 00:17:09.350
At first, the researchers were confused - had
they found another wreck, one of the other

00:17:09.350 --> 00:17:10.500
8 mentioned?

00:17:10.500 --> 00:17:16.140
Or perhaps the body of the monstrous creature
SCP-2406 had fallen in battle with.

00:17:16.140 --> 00:17:20.230
But after excavating it, they realized they
had found something they hadn’t even been

00:17:20.230 --> 00:17:25.630
looking for to begin with: SCP-2406’s left
arm.

00:17:25.630 --> 00:17:29.470
The way it landed suggested that it had been
torn off during the battle and hurled away

00:17:29.470 --> 00:17:34.200
- but what monster could possibly throw something
that heavy 30 entire kilometers?

00:17:34.200 --> 00:17:41.529
Either way, what the Foundation found attached
to SCP-2406’s arm is much more interesting.

00:17:41.529 --> 00:17:45.299
The researchers aren’t sure what it is,
but it’s much different from the rest of

00:17:45.299 --> 00:17:47.809
SCP-2406.

00:17:47.809 --> 00:17:52.940
It seems to be some kind of weapon, but one
that’s not made of any metals on Earth,

00:17:52.940 --> 00:17:55.559
and with an incredibly anomalous design.

00:17:55.559 --> 00:18:02.379
The Foundation personnel, not sure what to
make of it, designated it SCP-2406-1.

00:18:02.379 --> 00:18:08.420
Its purpose is similarly unknown and the consensus
seems to be that whatever it is, it far exceeds

00:18:08.420 --> 00:18:09.460
human understanding.

00:18:09.460 --> 00:18:14.850
But what the Foundation is sure of is that
it seems to bend reality near it, though they’re

00:18:14.850 --> 00:18:18.289
not sure how because it doesn’t seem to
affect anything.

00:18:18.289 --> 00:18:22.470
The Foundation’s best minds are stumped
by it - all they can say for certain is that

00:18:22.470 --> 00:18:28.429
if it was ever repaired, powered up, and activated,
it could do unprecedented damage to local

00:18:28.429 --> 00:18:29.429
reality.

00:18:29.429 --> 00:18:34.169
So any interaction with it was highly regulated
and the Foundation put it away with the rest

00:18:34.169 --> 00:18:37.179
of SCP-2406.

00:18:37.179 --> 00:18:44.039
Now go check out “SCP-2217 - Hammer And
Anvil” and “SCP-001 - The Broken God - Ouroboros

00:18:44.039 --> 00:18:47.160
Cycle” for more Anomalous Mekhanite Madness
from SCP Explained!

